@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml
title view-plan: execution-time targets and exact daily excesses
autonumber
participant "mishMash:MishMash" as App
participant "command:ViewPlanCommand" as Cmd
participant "mealPlanSource:Supplier" as Meals
participant "targetsSource:Supplier" as TargetSource
participant "active:ActiveMealPlan" as Active
participant "plan:MealPlan" as Plan

note over Cmd, TargetSource : Parser supplies both lambdas when constructing the command; parsing is omitted.
App -> Cmd : execute(book)
activate Cmd
Cmd -> Meals : get()
activate Meals
Meals -> Active : get()
Active --> Meals : optional plan
opt plan is present
  Meals -> Plan : toMealSummaries()
  Plan --> Meals : meals grouped by day
end
Meals --> Cmd : mealsByDay (empty if no plan)
deactivate Meals
create participant "viewer:MealPlanViewer" as Viewer
Cmd -> Viewer : new MealPlanViewer()
activate Viewer
Viewer --> Cmd : viewer
deactivate Viewer
alt mealsByDay is empty
  Cmd -> Viewer : view(mealsByDay)
  Viewer --> Cmd : no-active-plan message
  Cmd --> App : message
else selected day exceeds plan size
  Cmd --> App : throws MishMashException with view-plan usage
else all days or valid selected day
  Cmd -> TargetSource : get()
  activate TargetSource
  TargetSource -> Active : getRequest()
  Active --> TargetSource : optional generation request
  note right of TargetSource : Read request.targets(), or use\nNutritionTargets.none() if absent.
  TargetSource --> Cmd : targets
  deactivate TargetSource
  participant "targets:NutritionTargets" as Targets
  Cmd -> Viewer : view(mealsByDay, targets) or\nview(mealsByDay, dayNumber, targets)
  activate Viewer
  loop each displayed day only
    Viewer -> Viewer : formatDay(meals, dayNumber, targets)
    activate Viewer
    note right of Viewer
      formatDay first formats meals; formatDailyTotals then sums
      the day's MealSummary nutrition with mapToLong(...).sum().
      Construct NutritionTotals for actual daily values.
    end note
    Viewer -> Viewer : formatWarnings(totals, targets)
    activate Viewer
    Viewer -> Targets : calculateExcesses(totals)
    activate Targets
    note right of Targets
      For each nutrient: zero if target is null or actual <= target;
      otherwise actual - target. Generation tolerance is not applied.
      Construct a new NutritionTotals containing the excesses.
    end note
    Targets --> Viewer : excesses
    deactivate Targets
    note right of Viewer
      Read targets and excesses; formatWarning emits a line only for
      a positive excess. Order: calories, protein, carbs, fats.
      Place warnings after daily totals and before the closing separator.
    end note
    Viewer --> Viewer : warning lines, or empty string
    deactivate Viewer
    Viewer --> Viewer : formatted day
    deactivate Viewer
  end
  Viewer --> Cmd : formatted selection
  deactivate Viewer
  Cmd --> App : formatted selection
end
deactivate Cmd
note over Meals, Plan
  Supplier calls depict the default shared-state parser configuration.
  Null-source programming errors are omitted. An invalid upper day bound does not read targets.
  Empty-plan viewing delegates through the no-target overload; there is no active-state mutation.
end note
@enduml
